From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: video: realign the EL queue to the BL before toggling

amdv_parse_metadata_v2_stb() pairs each base-layer frame with whatever is at the
head of the dvel queue. It does not compare pts - FLAG_CHECK_ES_PTS is not in
dolby_vision_flags by default, so the check its code appears to make is compiled
in but never taken. So one base-layer frame that goes through unpaired leaves the
enhancement layer one frame behind for the rest of the title: every later
composite is built from the wrong EL, and nothing on this chain puts it back.

Measured on Avatar: Fire and Ash, 2026-09-07: exactly one "not found el" in five
hours, at the menu->feature segment transition. Steady-state playback produces
none. So this is not a timing problem to be waited out - it is a single
accounting error at a segment boundary that then persists.

The tree already has the right mechanism, in the wrong place.
recv_common_dequeue_frame() (video_receiver.c) asks dvbldec and dveldec for their
vf_put_count and drops the surplus EL frames before dequeuing the BL. That code
is unreachable for a Blu-ray: a profile-7 FEL title is forced to
STREAM_TYPE_STREAM, whose vfm chain is "dvbldec amlvideo deinterlace amvideo" and
terminates in amvideo, not video_render. Confirmed on-box in /sys/class/vfm/map.
So port it to the amvideo vsync path, at the same point relative to the dequeue.

Arithmetic, not timing: no held vsyncs, no dropped BL frames, no way to starve
the EL decoder. It fires only when bl_cnt > el_cnt, which is by definition a
surplus, so if the counts never diverge it is inert. That matters, because the
previous attempt at this bug tried to WAIT for the EL instead - which risked
back-pressuring the shared HEVC core, and in the event could never fire at all,
because vf_is_fel() requires a src_fmt the legacy h265 decoder never populates.

Two details worth keeping:

  - the format test accepts VFRAME_SIGNAL_FMT_INVALID, exactly as the
    video_receiver.c original does. The legacy decoder driving this chain never
    calls update_vframe_src_fmt(), so get_vframe_src_fmt() returns INVALID for
    every frame here and a DOVI-only test would never match.

  - the put-count query is req.vf == NULL, answered at
    frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c with atomic_read(&hevc->vf_put_count).
    aux_size is seeded with 0xffffffff so a provider that does not implement the
    query is detected rather than read as a count of zero.

The drop is logged. There is no measurement yet of how often the counts actually
diverge - only that they did once - so the log line is how we find out whether
this is load-bearing or inert on real discs.

Signed-off-by: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c
@@ -908,6 +908,114 @@
 	return vf;
 }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MEDIA_ENHANCEMENT_DOLBYVISION
+#ifndef DVEL_RECV_NAME
+#define DVEL_RECV_NAME "dvel"
+#endif
+
+/* Drop one surplus enhancement-layer frame.
+ *
+ * Lifted verbatim from video_receiver.c, where it is the back half of the only
+ * BL/EL realignment in the tree. That copy is unreachable here: it runs in
+ * recv_common_dequeue_frame(), i.e. the video_render receiver, and a profile-7
+ * FEL Blu-ray is forced to STREAM_TYPE_STREAM, whose vfm chain
+ * ("dvbldec amlvideo deinterlace amvideo") terminates in amvideo instead.
+ */
+static inline int recycle_dvel_vf_put(void)
+{
+	int event = 0, ret = 0;
+	struct vframe_s *vf = NULL;
+	struct vframe_provider_s *vfp = vf_get_provider(DVEL_RECV_NAME);
+
+	if (vfp) {
+		vf = vf_get(DVEL_RECV_NAME);
+		if (vf) {
+			vf_put(vf, DVEL_RECV_NAME);
+			event |= VFRAME_EVENT_RECEIVER_PUT;
+			vf_notify_provider(DVEL_RECV_NAME, event, NULL);
+			ret = 1;
+		}
+	}
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/* Re-pair the enhancement layer with the base layer before toggling.
+ *
+ * amdv_parse_metadata_v2_stb() takes whatever is at the head of the dvel queue
+ * for each BL, with no pts comparison (FLAG_CHECK_ES_PTS is not in
+ * dolby_vision_flags by default). So a single BL that goes through unpaired -
+ * measured once per disc, at the menu->feature segment transition - leaves the
+ * EL one frame behind for the REST of the title: every later composite is built
+ * from the wrong enhancement layer, and nothing on this chain corrects it.
+ *
+ * The decoders' own put counts say how far apart the layers are, so the fix is
+ * arithmetic rather than timing: drop the surplus. No held vsyncs, no dropped BL
+ * frames, no risk of starving the EL decoder - the failure mode of an earlier
+ * attempt that tried to WAIT for the EL instead, which additionally could never
+ * fire because vf_is_fel() requires a src_fmt this decoder never populates.
+ *
+ * Note the format test accepts VFRAME_SIGNAL_FMT_INVALID. That is deliberate and
+ * is what the video_receiver.c original does: the legacy h265 decoder driving
+ * this chain never calls update_vframe_src_fmt(), so get_vframe_src_fmt()
+ * returns INVALID for every frame here.
+ */
+static void dvel_realign_to_bl(struct vframe_s *vf)
+{
+	struct provider_aux_req_s req;
+	enum vframe_signal_fmt_e fmt;
+	u32 bl_cnt;
+	int i;
+
+	if (!vf || !is_amdv_enable())
+		return;
+
+	fmt = get_vframe_src_fmt(vf);
+	if (fmt != VFRAME_SIGNAL_FMT_DOVI &&
+	    fmt != VFRAME_SIGNAL_FMT_INVALID)
+		return;
+	if (!vf_peek(DVEL_RECV_NAME))
+		return;
+
+	/* req.vf == NULL is the put-count query: the decoder answers with
+	 * atomic_read(&hevc->vf_put_count) and returns. aux_size is seeded with
+	 * a sentinel so a provider that does not implement it is detected rather
+	 * than read as a count of zero.
+	 */
+	memset(&req, 0, sizeof(req));
+	req.aux_size = 0xffffffff;
+	vf_notify_provider_by_name("dvbldec",
+		VFRAME_EVENT_RECEIVER_GET_AUX_DATA, (void *)&req);
+	bl_cnt = req.aux_size;
+
+	memset(&req, 0, sizeof(req));
+	req.aux_size = 0xffffffff;
+	vf_notify_provider_by_name("dveldec",
+		VFRAME_EVENT_RECEIVER_GET_AUX_DATA, (void *)&req);
+
+	if (req.aux_size == 0xffffffff || bl_cnt == 0xffffffff ||
+	    bl_cnt <= req.aux_size)
+		return;
+
+	i = bl_cnt - req.aux_size;
+	/*
+	 * This runs from the vsync hard-IRQ, once per vsync. Any state where the
+	 * base layer stays ahead of a non-empty enhancement queue therefore
+	 * prints 50-120 lines a second on a release build - the function this
+	 * was lifted from (video_receiver.c) carries no log line at all.
+	 * Rate-limited so it still says what happened without becoming the
+	 * fault it is reporting.
+	 */
+	pr_info_ratelimited("dvel: bl %u el %u - dropping %d surplus el frame(s)\n",
+		bl_cnt, req.aux_size, i);
+	while (i > 0) {
+		if (!recycle_dvel_vf_put())
+			break;
+		i--;
+	}
+}
+#endif
+
+
 inline struct vframe_s *amvideo_vf_get(void)
 {
 	struct vframe_s *vf = NULL;
@@ -3943,6 +4043,12 @@
 			if (performance_debug & DEBUG_FLAG_VSYNC_PROCESS_TIME)
 				do_gettimeofday(&cur_line_info->end2);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MEDIA_ENHANCEMENT_DOLBYVISION
+			/* the BL is about to be toggled - make sure the EL that will be
+			 * paired with it in the parse is actually its own
+			 */
+			dvel_realign_to_bl(vf);
+#endif
 			vf = amvideo_vf_get();
 			if (!vf) {
 				ATRACE_COUNTER(MODULE_NAME,  __LINE__);
